* Legacy MPSA42 high-voltage NPN model.
* Source: the MPSA42/INF card in cmp\standard.bjt from a local LTspice Libraries
* folder (22 October 2026). The same file carries an MPSA43 card with identical
* parameters plus MFG=SIEMENS and VCEO=200, so this appears to be the same fit
* with its rating annotations stripped.
*
* Provenance and manufacturer fitting are unverified. This is not a
* manufacturer-provided model. BF=70.4 is consistent with the onsemi MPSA42
* datasheet minimum hFE of 40, and fT follows from TF=1.73n.
*
* NOTE: no BVcbo or BVbe is given, so this model has NO collector breakdown.
* The real MPSA42 is a 300 V part and will avalanche; the model will not, and
* will happily report collector voltages the device could never reach.
.MODEL MPSA42_LEGACY NPN( BF=7.04E+01 BR=1.76E+01 CJC=1.56E-11 CJE=1.31E-10
+ FC=5.00E-01 IKF=1.00E+01 IKR=1 IRB=1.30E-03 IS=1.59E-13 ISC=9.06E-11
+ ISE=3.62E-16 ITF=1.33 MJC=5.80E-01 MJE=4.02E-01 NC=1.47 NE=1.21E+00
+ NF=1.03E+00 NR=1.11 RB=3.23E+01 RBM=7.75E-02 RC=4.11E-01 RE=4.19E-01
+ TF=1.73n VAF=4.51E+01 VAR=9.11E+01 VJC=4.64E-01 VJE=3.00E-01 VTF=9.99E+05
+ XTB=0 XTF=1.00E+02 XTI=3 )
